---
source: workspace/acyclic-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help.stdout
---
The acyclic tracker. Every command prints one JSON document when piped and text for people at a terminal (`-o` chooses), except `prime`, `completions`, `graph` without `--file`, `import --schema` and help and version text

Usage: acyclic [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Common Commands:
  ready        Lists threads with ready work, the actor's own first, each with its ready items
  list         Lists every item, by id
  show         Shows items with their role, readiness and claims, and a parent's progress from its leaves, as an array in the order given
  claim        Claims a thread with ready work, or renews the actor's claim on it
  release      Releases the actor's claim on a thread, leaving anyone else's
  done         Marks an item done, with evidence
  needs        Lists what needs the user

Command Groups:
  item         Adds, edits, reopens, archives and deletes items
  link         Adds or removes links between items
  thread       Adds, edits, lists, shows, approves and revokes threads; agents' edits to approved scope wait as proposals
  repo         Adds, edits, lists and shows repository records
  proposal     Lists and shows proposals, and keeps or drops them (user only)

Other Commands:
  init         Sets up a tracker clone as a new replica, creating the repository if there is none
  sync         Fetches every replica's state from `origin`, joins it into this one, and pushes this replica's refs
  prime        Prints conventions for agents, matched to this version, as text
  import       Imports a plan, adding and updating what it names and never deleting; `--schema` prints an example
  graph        Draws the graph with threads as clusters: DOT or Mermaid, or an HTML page to open in a browser
  level        Prints the autonomy levels; with a level, sets the global one (user only)
  doctor       Lists entities that can't be read
  serve        Serves the JSON API and the app, refusing any request without the user's Tailscale identity
  up           Serves the JSON API and the app on this machine, to whoever holds its session
  completions  Prints a completion script for a shell, as text

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Global options:
      --tracker <TRACKER>  The tracker clone; otherwise `ACYCLIC_TRACKER`, else the clone you are in, else the mapping in ~/.config/acyclic/trackers.toml
      --actor <ACTOR>      Who acts; otherwise `ACYCLIC_ACTOR`, else `agent/undeclared`. The user must say so on the command
      --as-user            Act as the user
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>    How to print: the JSON envelope, or tables and summaries for people, with errors as text on standard error; otherwise `ACYCLIC_OUTPUT`, else pretty on a terminal and json when piped [possible values: json, pretty]

Run 'acyclic help <command>' for more information on a command.
